{"step_index":393,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T10:35:16Z","input_tokens":2571,"cache_read_tokens":223016,"output_tokens":1245,"content":"Here is a self-contained root script that cleans the stray files blocking `build-golden.sh`, updates the golden subvolume with the latest build artifacts, and executes the release deployment.\n\n### What the Script Does\n\n1. **Removes the stray helper files** in `/opt/op-dbus/golden/libexec/3tched/` (`op-chat-responder@.service` and `recover-3tchedfs`) that violate the golden helper manifest and cause `build-golden.sh` to halt.\n2. **Reseals and persists the plugin catalog** into `/var/lib/opdbus/plugin-blobs` and live SHM.\n3. **Prepares `/opt/op-dbus/golden`** using `deploy/lib/golden/build-golden.sh` so that the newly built `op-grpc-bridge` (which expects `chat_router`) replaces the stale binary in `golden`.\n4. **Deploys the release** into the inactive slot (`slot b`) via the approved release launcher.\n\n---\n\n### Root Script\n\nYou can save this to `/srv/git/odbus-verified/deploy-fix.sh` and run `sudo bash /srv/git/odbus-verified/deploy-fix.sh`:\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nREPO=\"/srv/git/odbus-verified\"\ncd \"$REPO\"\n\necho \"==> 1. Removing stray golden helpers...\"\nrm -f /opt/op-dbus/golden/libexec/3tched/op-chat-responder@.service\nrm -f /opt/op-dbus/golden/libexec/3tched/recover-3tchedfs\n\necho \"==> 2. Sealing and persisting catalog...\"\ntarget/release/opblob seal-shm\ntarget/release/opblob persist\n\necho \"==> 3. Running provision-slots...\"\n/usr/local/libexec/opdbus-release/op-release-launch provision-slots\n\necho \"==> 4. Preparing golden subvolume...\"\ndeploy/lib/golden/build-golden.sh\n\necho \"==> 5. Deploying and rotating to the new slot...\"\n/usr/local/libexec/opdbus-release/op-release-launch deploy\n\necho \"==> Deployment complete. Inspecting release status...\"\n/usr/local/libexec/opdbus-release/op-release-launch status\n```\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Do not pass `--system` to `/usr/local/libexec/opdbus-release/op-release-launch deploy`. The installed launcher strictly requires a single argument (`deploy`), and invoking it without `--system` allows the rotating overlay and services (`op-grpc-bridge`, `op-web`, `emqx`) to rotate and start cleanly.","thinking":"Comparing file hashes is crucial to determine if a deployment is needed, by checking if the current binaries match the pinned versions in the manifest. The shell script verifies if the deployed files are identical to the expected release versions, triggering an update if discrepancies exist. Discrepancies may indicate an outdated or corrupted deployment.\n\n\n"}
